 ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- Consider $\\lambda =-2.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-(-2)I & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -3\\end{aligned}]-(-2)[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 7 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking for nonzero solutions of $(A-(-2)I)x=0,$ we obtain the eigenvector \n\n$\\,$ ${v}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Step 3.** We construct the invertible matrix $P$ using our eigenvectors, as follows:\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139535748 true] [17592186364724 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364725 13194139535748 true] [17592186364724 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364726 13194139535748 true] [17592186364724 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364727 13194139535748 true] [17592186364724 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364728 13194139535748 true] [17592186364724 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364729 13194139535748 true] [17592186364724 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535748 true] [17592186364724 1041 "selection" 13194139535748 true] [17592186364724 1104 #edb/ref 17592186364726 13194139535748 true] [17592186364724 1110 #uuid "f1f6dfc9-5372-516c-9367-fab010319dec" 13194139535748 true] [17592186364725 1034 "P=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535748 true] [17592186364725 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535748 true] [17592186364725 1111 #uuid "9f2a5708-1e55-59c2-a757-3d1bbbfd4fc0" 13194139535748 true] [17592186364726 1034 "P=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535748 true] [17592186364726 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535748 true] [17592186364726 1111 #uuid "f5f4fae0-0c44-5ab0-98cc-9f7fe66b0149" 13194139535748 true] [17592186364727 1034 "P=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0